  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1036",
      "html": "<ul><li>Scientific name: Silurichthys hasseltii Bleeker, 1858</li><li>Common name: Hassel's Leaf Catfish</li><li>Type locality: Tjisekat, Java, Indonesia.</li><li>Size: 110 mm (4.3\") SL.</li><li>Identification: Distinguished by a shorter caudal fin, more mottled coloration, 2-4 gill rakers on first branchial arch and 46-56 anal-fin rays.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1036",
      "html": "<p>Asia: Malaysia, Singapore and Indonesia. Known from the Mekong basin. IUCN Red List category: Least Concern (last assessed 2019).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1036",
      "html": "<ul><li>pH: 5.2 - 7.0</li><li>Temperature: 22.0-27.0°C (71.6-80.6°F)</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1036",
      "html": "<p>Provide plenty of driftwood as hiding places. They also enjoy a layer of leaf litter to burrow into.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1036",
      "html": "<p>Will eat all manner of live, frozen and prepared foods.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1036",
      "html": "<p>A peaceful, shoaling species compatible with most fish. Ideal tankmates are mid-sized barbs, rasboras and gouramies in an Asian forest stream biotope tank.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1036",
      "html": "<p>Males are smaller and possess serrations on posterior edge of pectoral spine.</p>"
    },
    {
